# ARK Router — Cursor Rules

## Project Scope
ARK Router is an OpenWrt LuCI application and modern dark theme for embedded routers (OpenWrt 19.07 to 25.x).

## Core Principles
- **Backend**: Pure POSIX shell (`/bin/sh` with BusyBox ash). Zero bashisms (`[[ ]]`, `${var//}`, arrays). Atomic UCI commits (`uci commit network`).
- **Frontend**: Vanilla JavaScript LuCI SPA views (`L.view.extend`, `ui.*`, CBI widgets). Zero heavy runtime npm dependencies.
- **Hardware Constraints**: Maintain > 80 MB free RAM (128 MB devices) and > 2 MB free in `/overlay`. Never write logs to Flash; use `/tmp`.
- **Modular Rules**: Specialized guidelines are defined in `.cursor/rules/`:
  - `ark-router-luci.mdc`: LuCI client views, DOM handling, and RPC.
  - `openwrt-shell-uci.mdc`: POSIX shell, UCI configuration, and service daemons.
  - `ark-theme-design.mdc`: Theme colors, mobile-first touch targets (40px), and CSS containment.
- **Canonical Guidelines**: Refer to `AGENTS.md` for complete architecture and validation runbooks.
